  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Hecatombe, a limited edition artist's book, is a response to the 9-11 attacks on the United States. The structure of the book symbolically reflects the two towers, which are connected by a wall of images in the center accordion structure. The photographs were taken by the artist and the victim's names are from the web site http://www.september11victims.com designed by Alex Spektor. ... The book was written, designed and printed by the artist. The text and images are laser printed, using Mohawk for the accordion images, Fabriano Tiziano for the endsheets, and Pergamena for the covers. The cover title is laser stenciled to create a void. The end sheets are relief printed"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Front and back sections have hand-sewn exposed spine binding and are connected by twelve plates glued into an accordion fold construction. Issued in a handmade illustrated box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 50.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC has copy 22 signed by the book artist.</subfield>
    <subfield code="5">DLC</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="530" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Full list of victim's names also issued online.</subfield>
  </datafield>
